    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "watching clouds won't fix the fact that i have zero control. everything is decided for me—when i wake up, when i eat, how much i'm worth per hour. it's like i'm pretending to be a person, but i'm really just a ghost inhabiting a uniform. i just want to feel like i actually own my life for once, but how is that even possible when the machine is so much bigger than me?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
